    "summary": "Laiili tending to an emaciated Majnun; single-page painting on an album folio. Majnun, covered  by only a cloth around his waist, lays upon Laili, gazing up at her. Laili, dressed in printed jacket, skirt, and pants, sits cross-legged, supporting Majnun. Surrounding them rest a dog, lion, gazelle, and rabbit. Inscribed. Album contains 44 paintings and drawings, mostly of Persian costumes and animals with some drawings by Kaempfer.\r\nInk and opaque watercolour on paper. Album is bound in brown leather with gold gilt  decoration. Inside covers have marbled paper.",
